  "state_definition": "Per account, retain event-time ordered (beneficiary, day, event_id) entries for trailing inclusive 7-day interval; remove entries where day < current_day-6; count distinct beneficiaries; flag at >=3.",
  "scale_design": "Partition stream state by account key within each data-residency region; process local identifiers locally; export only approved aggregate alert statistics. Consider approximate distinct sketches only if false-positive/false-negative bounds are acceptable; hot-account skew needs salting or dedicated state shards.",
  "reflection": "Adding machines helps only when work can be partitioned. The keyed detector reduces repeated cross-account comparisons, but one highly active account remains a hot key, state and shuffle still grow, and coordination or I/O can dominate. Our 10k\u20131m keyed runs show linear input processing, while the naive method requires n\u00b2 comparisons (100 million at 10k and 10^12 at 1m). More workers cannot remove a serial bottleneck or data skew; partitioning, state bounds and locality must be designed first."
